<GuideLayout 
  title="The B2B Manufacturing Timeline: From Design to Delivery" 
  type="TIMELINE"
  description="Manage your expectations. A detailed breakdown of the time required for sampling, mass production, and global shipping."
>
  <h2>Planning Your Collection Launch</h2>
  <p>One of the biggest mistakes new brands make is underestimating the time required for manufacturing. A professional collection typically takes 3-4 months from concept to doorstep.</p>
  
  <h3>Phase 1: Development & Sampling (2-4 Weeks)</h3>
  <p>This includes finalizing tech packs, fabric sourcing, and creating the first Proto sample. If multiple revisions are needed, this phase can extend.</p>

  <h3>Phase 2: Mass Production (4-6 Weeks)</h3>
  <p>Once the PPS (Pre-Production Sample) is approved, mass production begins. This includes fabric knitting/dyeing, cutting, sewing, and final quality control inspections.</p>

  <h3>Phase 3: Quality Control & Packing (1 Week)</h3>
  <p>Every piece is inspected, trimmed, ironed, and packed into your custom branded packaging.</p>

  <h3>Phase 4: Global Shipping (1-4 Weeks)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Air Freight:</strong> 5-9 days (Faster but more expensive)</li>
    <li><strong>Sea Freight:</strong> 25-35 days (Economical for bulk orders)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Pro Tip: Peak Seasons</h3>
  <p>Always add 2-3 weeks to your timeline if you are producing around major holidays like Chinese New Year or the October National Day, as logistics networks often become congested.</p>
</GuideLayout>
